{"timestamp": "2023-11-30T02:05:00+00:00", "time_ago": "5d ago", "role": "user", "relevance": {"rrf_score": 0.3333333333333333, "fts_rank": 3}, "content": "That's really helpful! I think I'll start with infusing gin with cucumber and mint separately to see how the flavors develop. By the way, speaking of gin, I recently hosted a dinner party and served a Cranberry Sparkler, which was a huge hit. I've also been perfecting my Negroni game - I've tried making it at home 10 times now since my friend Emma showed me how to make it. Do you have any recommendations for other classic cocktails that I should try making?"}
{"timestamp": "2023-08-11T17:15:00+00:00", "time_ago": "116d ago", "role": "user", "relevance": {"rrf_score": 0.25, "fts_rank": 4}, "content": "That's really helpful, thanks! I'll definitely try out that lavender syrup recipe and experiment with the cocktails you suggested. By the way, speaking of experimenting with cocktails, I've been trying to perfect my Negroni recipe and I've found that using Hendrick's gin and Carpano Antica vermouth really brings out the flavors. I've tried making it at home for 5 times now since Emma teached me how to make it, and I'm getting closer to getting it just right. Do you have any recommendations for other bitter liqueurs I could try in place of Campari?"}
